{
  "_why": "MrCrayfish's Furniture Mod: Refurbished for the Safe Zones: stair seats become chairs and sofas, table tops become tables, counters and storage become the mod's counters, drawers and crates, wool beds become its beds, when the mod 'refurbished_furniture' is loaded. THE IDS BELOW ARE NOT VERIFIED (no copy of the mod was available when this was written): every plausible spelling is listed in order of likelihood, the first one that exists in the block registry is used, and when none exists the vanilla block stays. {wood} is filled from the block being replaced (dark_oak_stairs gives dark_oak, default oak) and {color} from a coloured block (default red). Open the mod's jar (assets/refurbished_furniture/blockstates) and edit this list to the real ids: no rebuild needed. flip_facing lists the hints whose `facing` must be reversed (a stair 'faces' up its slope, behind the sitter; a chair faces the way the sitter looks). facing_property is the name of the replacement's horizontal facing property (vanilla style: facing).",
  "mod": "refurbished_furniture",
